> hmmm, is there a construct for saying "55 give or take x"?  That would be
> quite handy.  Especially if you could put {so'u} and friends in for "x" to
> get some fuzziness to the "about 55" statement.
.skamyxatra

Yes, "{mumu mi'i xy}," meaning "within x (units) of 55."  However, if you want
to use it as a quantifier (and not a "{li}" {sumti}), you have to precede it
with "{vei}."

